      "t": "平土有叢木曰林。从二木。凡林之屬皆从林。",
      "w": 1
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Duplication of 木 (“tree”) to give the idea of multiple trees (compare 森), thus a forest. See also the top component of 散 in its original version.\nFrom Proto-Sino-Tibetan *rəm (“jungle; forest; country; field”) (STEDT under PTB *ram). Cognate with 森 (OC *srɯm, “forest”), Mizo ram (“forest; country”), Karbi ram (“jungle”).\nOr perhaps an area word (Schuessler, 2007), shared with Khmer រាម (riəm, “thick bushy jungle that grows along a stream”), Old Khmer *rām (“inundated forest along a watercourse”), Old Khmer sarāma ~ sarāṃ (“a tract of stunted vegetation”), Mon ရာံ (rèm, “copse; patch of woodland”)."
    }
  ],
  "shuowen": "平土有叢木曰林。从二木。凡林之屬皆从林。",
  "shuowenExplanation": "平土有叢木 is called 林. Composed with 二木. All characters in the 林 category contain 林 as radical.",
